Subject: Restore whole original camera source for native production

Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Restore CameraMan, DebugCam and animcam directly from the pinned reconstructed
source, including ordinary camera allocations, source callbacks/factories,
filters, original global construction and the local frontend asset catalog.
Keep prototype camera ownership, constructor writes, deleted copying and
checked playback/controls only under an explicit diagnostic camera profile.
Require that profile for extracted camera helpers and reject it in game modules.

Retain the existing native unsigned 32-bit noise transport that implements the
original Wii wraparound. Restore original filter requests and Reset behavior;
extra validation and initialization are diagnostic only. A native complete-type
include satisfies immediate checking of the original DrawableCharacter Replay
template; its pointer carrier and original source algorithms are unchanged.

This corrects source selection and compilation. It does not establish full
camera data decoding, source/provider lifetime, gameplay or scene startup.

Refreshed for decomp 9046e67a: src/Game/Camera/CameraMan.cpp keeps its upstream
text throughout, so this patch no longer touches it.

